message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PCC-VizForge: reproducible simulation, statistical inference and visualisation for canonical stochastic processes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Praveen
    given-names: Satvik
    email: satvikpraveen707@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/PCC-VizForge"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
keywords:
  - stochastic processes
  - synthetic data
  - anomalous diffusion
  - fractional Brownian motion
  - Gutenberg-Richter law
  - ETAS
  - power-law distributions
  - weather generator
  - reproducibility
  - visualization
abstract: >-
  PCC-VizForge generates synthetic data from five canonical stochastic
  models (random walks and fractional Brownian motion, dice, ETAS-style
  earthquake catalogues, WGEN-type daily weather, and heavy-tailed
  repository popularity), estimates their parameters with standard
  field-specific estimators, and records every run with a provenance
  manifest so it can be regenerated bit-for-bit. Monte Carlo validation
  studies report the bias, RMSE and confidence-interval coverage of each
  estimator against known ground truth.
